1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,022
Walk into this bank

2
00:00:01,068 --> 00:00:02,067
with a million dollars.

3
00:00:02,125 --> 00:00:03,251
They'll turn you away.

4
00:00:03,692 --> 00:00:05,004
Private banking here starts

5
00:00:05,039 --> 00:00:06,026
at a minimum most

6
00:00:06,084 --> 00:00:07,303
millionaires never reach.

7
00:00:07,686 --> 00:00:09,300
The entry threshold typically

8
00:00:09,334 --> 00:00:10,426
starts around ten million

9
00:00:10,472 --> 00:00:11,517
dollars in assets.

10
00:00:11,958 --> 00:00:13,270
Clients above that line

11
00:00:13,317 --> 00:00:14,362
pay a management fee

12
00:00:14,408 --> 00:00:15,859
near one percent a year.

13
00:00:16,184 --> 00:00:17,392
In exchange, a single

14
00:00:17,438 --> 00:00:18,576
banker handles everything:

15
00:00:19,017 --> 00:00:21,780
tax, property, even art purchases.

16
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:23,673
That relationship alone can

17
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:24,776
be worth over fifty

18
00:00:24,834 --> 00:00:25,774
thousand dollars a year

19
00:00:25,821 --> 00:00:26,459
in service.

20
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:27,771
The money was never

21
00:00:27,829 --> 00:00:28,677
really the product.

22
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:30,209
The access was.

23
00:00:30,592 --> 00:00:31,626
So the account minimum

24
00:00:31,672 --> 00:00:32,450
was never really about

25
00:00:32,485 --> 00:00:33,170
the money in it.

26
00:00:33,495 --> 00:00:34,191
It was about who

27
00:00:34,249 --> 00:00:34,969
gets to call.

28
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:36,780
Follow for more of these.
